Dialogs keep their contents, and roles/offices are multi-selects

- Clicking outside a dialog (or pressing Escape) discarded a half-filled
  form without warning. On "add project", with dozens of fields, that
  meant starting over. Dismissal is explicit now — the ✕ or Cancel — and
  `dismissable` opts back in for display-only dialogs.
- Roles and offices were open rows of checkboxes that grew the form by
  several lines and buried the selected ones among the unselected. They
  are fields now: chips for what is chosen, a list on click.
- Office membership and office management are separate fields. They were
  two checkboxes on one row, which read as one setting with a modifier
  rather than two independent facts.
- Sections are separated by a dashed frame, matching the existing-user
  block.

